What is Dependency Injection (DI)
DI means Spring provides objects (dependencies) to your class instead of you creating them.

Constructor injection → immutable, testable, recommended
Field injection → harder to test, reflection-based
Constructor injection is the recommended approach where dependencies are provided through the constructor, making them immutable and easier to test. Field injection uses reflection to inject dependencies directly into fields, which makes testing harder and doesn’t enforce required dependencies.

